{"body":"Target-derived safety incident from 2026-08-12 19:10 PDT.\r\n\r\nContext:\r\n- nimo-2 protected production RPC worker owned about 114,041,696 KiB of kernel-tracked gpu_active/HMM pages.\r\n- MemAvailable appeared to be about 14-17 GB.\r\n- An isolated source build of candidate e1023132 used Ninja -j2. The observed cc1plus processes were only tens of MiB RSS at the OOM snapshots.\r\n\r\nObserved failure:\r\n- The kernel repeatedly invoked the global OOM killer.\r\n- It first killed user-session processes, then PID 2148915 ggml-rpc-server.\r\n- systemd recorded Result=oom-kill and restarted the worker.\r\n- The coordinator health endpoint remained superficially healthy until a one-token recovery probe exercised RPC; the stale connection aborted the coordinator, and systemd restarted it so the model could be reloaded across both ranks.\r\n- The candidate build was terminated immediately and no benchmark result was retained.\r\n\r\nExact kernel evidence included gpu_active:114041696kB, about 14,405,396 KiB free in Normal, and the worker large HMM address space. Ordinary MemAvailable was therefore not a safe target admission signal.\r\n\r\nRequired project change:\r\n- Never build, quantize, or start disposable test workloads on either target while protected production owns KFD/render/HMM resources.\r\n- Target test admission must require an authorized production maintenance window, exact absence of foreign GPU owners, protected service/PID checks, and a retained pre-run kernel OOM baseline. MemAvailable alone must never authorize work.\r\n- A worker restart invalidates coordinator RPC state; recovery verification must exercise a real minimal inference, not only /health.\r\n- Preserve this incident in the adapter/preflight documentation and add deterministic refusal tests.\r\n\r\nNo performance claim is made. This issue tracks the safety guard and evidence; it does not authorize stopping production.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOT2ckv88AAAABOmzawA","author":{"login":"JCFrags"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Recovery evidence at 2026-08-12 19:16 PDT:\r\n- nimo-1 coordinator: PID 3113343, InvocationID 0656332b63a140eab7214627baa43253, NRestarts=1, health HTTP 200.\r\n- nimo-2 worker: PID 2248760, InvocationID d15fe49610274e77bd9a3d84a0b791a5, NRestarts=1, listener active.\r\n- A real recovery probe evaluated 5 prompt tokens and generated 1 token successfully over the dual-rank path.\r\n- No interrupted build process remained.\r\n\r\nThis confirms recovery after both systemd restarts. It does not make concurrent target work safe; target performance work remains gated on isolated maintenance admission.","createdAt":"2026-08-13T02:20:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JCFrags/HaloFPX/issues/41#issuecomment-5275179712","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"labels":[],"number":41,"state":"OPEN","title":"P0: Reject target work while production owns HMM pages","url":"https://github.com/JCFrags/HaloFPX/issues/41"}
